  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Trochoidal slot with a selection picked (a face or edge chains) generated a path across the selected pocket's wall into the model and reported **OK** (#1503, maintainer screenshot). Generation now refuses such a slot by name, with the numbers:\n\n> Trochoidal slot: the 16.000 mm wide slot from A (-20.000, 0.000) to B (20.000, 0.000) does not fit its selection - it needs 8.000 mm clear each side of its centre line, but the selection's edge comes within 5.000 mm at (...), so the cut would run 3.000 mm past the selection into the model; shorten or narrow the slot, or select the region it should cut\n\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/slot_fit.rs`: `refuse_unfit_slot(kind, a, b, width, region)`. This is pure plane geometry. The slot's capsule (centre line A-B, half-width width/2) must lie inside the picked region: both endpoints inside, and every boundary edge of every loop (holes included) at least width/2 from the centre line, with 1e-4 mm of slack so a slot exactly as wide as its pocket still fits. The generator already keeps every loop inside that band (`contained` in motion `trochoid_slot`), so the check covers what is cut. It refuses rather than clips, which is simpler and safe.\n- `operation/generate.rs`: the TrochoidalSlot arm resolves its region first. When the source is a selection, it calls the helper before generating.\n- No selection: nothing changes. The typed endpoints rule, and the post judges the path against the model.\n\n**Step 0 (posted on #1503):** on upstream main df90b031 the post **already refused** this slot through the stock-sim gouge clause: `gouge: program cuts below the model in 5926 cell(s), worst 20.00 mm at (-25.31, -5.94, z 0.00)`. The gap was at generation, where the status was `ok` with cached blocking `Gouge` findings. Nothing opts this op out of the gouge check. The page text \"Boundary settings do not apply\" only means the area controls (offset, extension) are not used.\n\n**Shared with #1504:** the helper takes the kind's label, so the plain Slot can call it unchanged. Slot is excluded in `selection_drives_region`, so its arm sees the authored stadium today, not the picks; #1504 (M3) owns that. Noted on #1503 and #1504. The Slot arm is not touched here.\n\n**Split:** Expected item 2 (trochoidal motion as a 2D Adaptive method) is out of this PR. It is filed as #1509 (Part of #1503, effort:max). That is why this PR says `Refs #1503`, not Fixes: #1503's Done means includes the Adaptive method. The maintainer can close #1503 when this merges if #1509 carries item 2.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/trochoid_confine.rs`. The fixture is an 80 x 60 x 20 block with a 50 x 25 pocket to z 10 (floor face 1250 mm2, as in the screenshot) and a 6 mm `EM-0600-4FL`.\n\n| Pin | What it holds |\n|---|---|\n| `a_slot_longer_than_its_selected_pocket_face_is_refused_by_name` | The screenshot setup (A (-20,0), B (20,0), width 16, floor face picked) is refused by name with 8.000 / 5.000 / 3.000. No path is cached and nothing posts. |\n| `mcp_refuses_the_same_slot_by_name` | The same refusal over MCP: `add_operation` (seeded A/B/width), `set_operation_geometry` (floor face), `generate`. The post is refused too. |\n| `a_slot_that_fits_its_selection_generates_and_posts_clean` | A (-12,0) to B (12,0), width 16 generates with no blocking warning. The program gate (stock sim against the model) is empty and it posts. No false refusal. |\n| `the_post_refuses_an_unconfined_trochoid_that_enters_the_model` | With no selection, the same slot through the end walls generates, and the post's stock-sim gouge clause refuses it (`gouge: program cuts below the model ...`). |\n| `slot_fit::tests` (unit, 2) | Fits, exactly-as-wide fits, past the end wall refused with numbers, endpoint outside, centre line across a hole. |\n\nMutation checks (revert the guard, confirm red, restore, confirm green):\n- Confinement call disabled (`if false && ...` in generate.rs): `a_slot_longer...` and `mcp_refuses...` are **red**, the other two green. Restored: 4/4 green.\n- Sim gouge clause blinded (`Ok(sim) if false && sim.dev.gouge_cells > 0` in posting_sim.rs): `the_post_refuses...` is **red**, the others green. Restored: 4/4 green.\n- Guard made 5 mm too strict (`d + FIT_TOL < half + 5.0`): `a_slot_that_fits...` is **red** (a false refusal is caught). Restored: 4/4 green.\n\nGates (local, macOS, fork synced at upstream main df90b031): the quick gate's app step (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, 167 app suites incl. trochoid_op, trochoid_confine, operations, posting, mcp, mcp_order, stock_sim_document, slot_caps, pocket_overhead, plus mcp_verify, mcp_pick, mcp_pockets, pocket_recognition) all green, and `camcraft-app --lib` 186/186 after a fix to my own unit fixture. motion `trochoid_slot` green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. The quick gate's ui step (boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, feedback, machine, operations, sinker_setup) was **not run**: no ui code changed, and those suites open windows.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI page text (\"Boundary settings do not apply to it\") is unchanged. The structural UI test is not touched, and the ui suites were not run (no ui code changed; they open windows).\n- Depth: a slot whose bottom is below the picked floor face is not refused at generation. The verify pass caches blocking `Gouge` findings and the post's sim refuses it, as for every other op.\n- Edge-chain selections go through the same picked region. Only the face pick is pinned.\n\nChangelog: A Trochoidal slot with a selection is refused by name, with the numbers, when its endpoints and width do not fit inside the selected region, instead of generating across a wall into the model (#1503)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1503\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
